#Tuition policy

Tuition is paid per semester; the graduate program charges fees paid at registration. Students may apply for installment plans, late fee waivers, and payment deadlines by the semester schedule. The tuition policy states that all charges are due before the add/drop period ends, and students who fail to pay may be withheld from official transcripts and registration. The university supports payment plans for all eligible students, with scholarship reductions applied before final billing. Students should check the portal each semester for updated rates. This document explains the due dates, processing steps, and exceptions for enrolled students. Tuition is paid per semester; the graduate program charges fees paid at registration. Students may apply for installment plans, late fee waivers, and payment deadlines by the semester schedule. The tuition policy states that all charges are due before the add/drop period ends, and students who fail to pay may be withheld from official transcripts and registration. The university supports payment plans for all eligible students, with scholarship reductions applied before final billing. Students should check the portal each semester for updated rates. This document explains the due dates, processing steps, and exceptions for enrolled students. Tuition is paid per semester; the graduate program charges fees paid at registration. Students may apply for installment plans, late fee waivers, and payment deadlines by the semester schedule. The tuition policy states that all charges are due before the add/drop period ends, and students who fail to pay may be withheld from official transcripts and registration. The university supports payment plans for all eligible students, with scholarship reductions applied before final billing. Students should check the portal each semester for updated rates. This document explains the due dates, processing steps, and exceptions for enrolled students. Tuition is paid per semester; the graduate program